<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">O'Connor Kerry</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ó Conchobhair Chiarraí</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The O'Connor Kerry, in Irish Ó Conchobhair Chiarraí, were the ruling family of the Ciarraige Luachra in north Kerry, Ireland, from the 11th century. Pushed northwards by the Anglo-Norman FitzGeralds in the 13th century, they held the territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraghticonnor">Iraghticonnor</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tralee">Tralee</a> and the Shannon, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrigafoyle-castle">Carrigafoyle Castle</a>. Their lands were largely lost after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desmond-rebellions">Desmond Rebellions</a> and the wars of the 17th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oconnor-kerry.jpg" alt="O'Connor Kerry" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: self-created · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O%27Conor.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
